---
layout: landing.njk
title: OPE
---
{# ABOUTME: OPE landing page: what the protocol does, four story walkthroughs, and the entitlement builder. #}
{# ABOUTME: Copy tracks the v0.2 specification (revision 5); stories map to its acceptance stories S1, S2, and S4. #}

{% macro storyDeck(id, label, cards, hidden) %}
<div class="story-deck{% if hidden %} hidden{% endif %}" id="story-{{ id }}" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-{{ id }}" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="{{ label }}">
  <div class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="deck-track flex transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out" style="transform: translateX(0)">
      {% for card in cards %}
      <div class="deck-card flex-none w-full px-1" role="group" aria-roledescription="slide">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5 p-6 sm:p-8 h-full">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-emerald-700">{{ loop.index }} of {{ cards | length }}</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">{{ card.title }}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">{{ card.body | safe }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-6">
    <div class="flex gap-1.5 deck-dots" role="group" aria-label="Slide navigation">
      {% for card in cards %}
      <button class="deck-dot w-2 h-2 rounded-full transition-colors {% if loop.first %}bg-emerald-500{% else %}bg-zinc-300{% endif %}" data-index="{{ loop.index0 }}" aria-label="Go to slide {{ loop.index }}"></button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="flex gap-2">
      <button class="deck-prev w-9 h-9 rounded-full ring-1 ring-zinc-900/10 flex items-center justify-center text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-900 transition-colors disabled:opacity-30" disabled aria-label="Previous slide">
        <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 12L6 8l4-4"/></svg>
      </button>
      <button class="deck-next w-9 h-9 rounded-full ring-1 ring-zinc-900/10 flex items-center justify-center text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-900 transition-colors disabled:opacity-30" aria-label="Next slide">
        <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 12l4-4-4-4"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sr-only deck-live" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-zinc-900 py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none opacity-30" aria-hidden="true" style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 50% at 50% -10%, #36b49f, transparent), radial-gradient(ellipse 40% 40% at 80% 100%, #DBFF75, transparent)"></div>
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 relative">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-400/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-emerald-400 ring-1 ring-inset ring-emerald-400/20">Draft v0.2 · Proposed, open for comment</span>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Your access, in every app</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed max-w-lg">Buy from a publisher once. Use it in any app you choose.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed max-w-lg">OPE is an open protocol, built on OAuth 2.0, for proving that a person holds access to something (an article, a podcast episode, a course, a pro feature) and carrying that proof across the apps they use. Feed readers, podcast players, editors, and browsers all check it the same way. No lock-in. No walled gardens.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="{{ '/ope/spec/0.2/' | url }}" class="rounded-full bg-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 hover:bg-emerald-400 no-underline transition-colors">Read the v0.2 Draft</a>
        <a href="{{ '/ope/demo/' | url }}" class="rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-300 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-400/20 hover:text-white hover:ring-zinc-400/40 no-underline transition-colors">See it working</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/shellen/open-portable-entitlement" class="rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-400 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-400/20 hover:text-white hover:ring-zinc-400/40 no-underline transition-colors">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed max-w-lg">This page describes v0.2, a proposed revision open for public comment until {{ spec.commentsUntil }}. The published version is still <a href="{{ '/ope/spec/' | url }}" class="text-zinc-300 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-white">v0.1</a>. <a href="{{ spec.commentsUrl }}" class="text-zinc-300 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-white">Tell us what you think</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Principles -->
<section class="border-b border-zinc-900/5 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-10">
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-400/10 text-emerald-700 mb-4">
          <svg width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 18.3s6.7-3.3 6.7-8.3V4.2L10 1.7 3.3 4.2V10c0 5 6.7 8.3 6.7 8.3z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Entitlement, not payments</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">OPE proves you're allowed in. Payment processors handle money. Clean separation.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-400/10 text-emerald-700 mb-4">
          <svg width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="2"/><path d="M13 18V4a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H9a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Truly portable</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">What you hold works in any OPE-compatible app: feed reader, podcast player, browser, or the tool you already use. No platform lock-in.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-400/10 text-emerald-700 mb-4">
          <svg width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3.3 9.2a7.5 7.5 0 0 1 7.5 7.5"/><path d="M3.3 3.3a13.3 13.3 0 0 1 13.3 13.3"/><circle cx="4.2" cy="15.8" r=".8"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Works with any feed</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">RSS, Atom, and JSON Feed today, with AT Protocol planned. OPE extends what you already use, and works without a feed too.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-400/10 text-emerald-700 mb-4">
          <svg width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6.5" cy="13.5" r="3.5"/><path d="M9 11l8-8"/><path d="M14 6l2 2"/><path d="M12 8l2 2"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Built on OAuth</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">OAuth 2.0 and its published RFCs, plus a few claims that say what a person holds. Nothing exotic to implement.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-emerald-400/10 text-emerald-700 mb-4">
          <svg width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14.2 17.5v-1.7a3.3 3.3 0 0 0-3.3-3.3H4.2a3.3 3.3 0 0 0-3.3 3.3v1.7"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="5.8" r="3.3"/><path d="M19.2 17.5v-1.7a3.3 3.3 0 0 0-2.5-3.2"/><path d="M13.3 2.6a3.3 3.3 0 0 1 0 6.5"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Publisher-controlled</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">Publishers decide who's entitled, for how long, and can end it. Their content, their rules.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Design Philosophy -->
<section class="py-20" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Design Philosophy</h2>
      <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Four layers, cleanly separated</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mt-3">OPE occupies the space between distribution and payment. Each concern stays independent.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <div class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-500 mb-2">Layer 1</div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Content</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">Articles, podcasts, video, courses, software features, and APIs. Created and served by the publisher.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <div class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-500 mb-2">Layer 2</div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Distribution</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">Feeds (RSS, Atom, JSON Feed), web pages, and apps that deliver previews and point to the full thing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-400/30 bg-emerald-400/5">
        <div class="text-xs font-medium text-emerald-700 mb-2">Layer 3: OPE</div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Entitlement</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">Proof that a person holds access, issued by the publisher's License Server and checked by its servers. Portable across apps.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5">
        <div class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-500 mb-2">Layer 4</div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">Payments</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">How money changes hands. Stripe, x402, Lightning, or anything else. Out of scope.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Flow -->
<section class="py-20 border-t border-zinc-900/5">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">The Flow</h2>
      <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">From a locked preview to the full thing</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mt-3">Five steps, all standard OAuth except the parts that describe what a person holds.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-8">
      {% for step in [
        {t:"Find", d:"An app meets something gated: a feed item, a web page, or a 401 or 402 from an API."},
        {t:"Discover", d:"It fetches the publisher's resource metadata (RFC 9728): what's on offer, and which License Server issues access."},
        {t:"Authorize", d:"The person signs in with that License Server through OAuth 2.0 with PKCE, and approves this app."},
        {t:"License Token", d:"The License Server issues a signed License Token for the item, or for everything the person's subscription covers."},
        {t:"Access", d:"The app presents the token. The publisher's server checks it and serves the article, episode, or feature."}
      ] %}
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full ring-1 ring-zinc-900/10 text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-700 mb-4">{{ loop.index }}</div>
        <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-1">{{ step.t }}</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">{{ step.d }}</p>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Stories -->
<section class="py-20 border-t border-zinc-900/5" id="stories">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">See It In Action</h2>
      <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">How OPE works for real people</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mt-3">A newsletter, a pro feature, a podcast, and a school course. Same protocol each time. Flip through to see how it works.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8" id="story-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Story examples">
      {% for tab in [
        {id:"alice", label:"Alice reads a newsletter"},
        {id:"priya", label:"Priya uses a pro feature"},
        {id:"bob", label:"Bob listens to a podcast"},
        {id:"school", label:"A school buys a course"}
      ] %}
      <button class="story-tab rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold transition-colors {% if loop.first %}bg-emerald-500 text-zinc-900{% else %}text-zinc-500 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-900/10 hover:text-zinc-900{% endif %}" data-story="{{ tab.id }}" role="tab" aria-selected="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}" aria-controls="story-{{ tab.id }}" id="tab-{{ tab.id }}"{% if not loop.first %} tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>{{ tab.label }}</button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {{ storyDeck("alice", "Alice's story walkthrough", [
      {title:"Alice follows a newsletter", body:"Alice adds <strong>The Lamplighter</strong> to her feed reader. Free issues show in full. Paid issues, like <em>\"Issue 42: Night Trains\"</em>, show their first three paragraphs and a note: paid subscribers read the rest."},
      {title:"Her reader finds the offer", body:"The feed carries one <code>ope:offer</code> for every paid issue: <strong>\"The Lamplighter, paid, $6/month.\"</strong> The reader checks it against the publisher's resource metadata, which also names the License Server to use. No special deal between this reader and this publisher."},
      {title:"Alice subscribes", body:"She taps <strong>Subscribe</strong>. The reader opens the publisher's own checkout in her browser, and she pays with whatever the publisher accepts. Back in the reader, she taps <strong>Unlock</strong>."},
      {title:"One sign-in, one token", body:"The reader sends her through a quick OAuth sign-in. The consent screen names the reader, the subscription, and the publisher's terms. She gets a <strong>License Token</strong> covering every paid issue, not just this one."},
      {title:"Every issue unlocks", body:"The reader presents the same token for each paid issue, and the publisher's server checks it each time. New issues arrive unlocked. The token refreshes quietly in the background."},
      {title:"A second reader, no second subscription", body:"Alice tries a different reader on her tablet. She signs in and approves that app, and it gets its own token for the <strong>same subscription</strong>. If she ever cancels, both stop working within the hour."}
    ], false) }}

    {{ storyDeck("priya", "Priya's story walkthrough", [
      {title:"Priya pays for Inkwell Pro", body:"Priya subscribes to <strong>Inkwell Pro</strong>, the paid tier of a writing tool, for $8/month. Pro includes <strong>pro export</strong>: polished PDFs and EPUBs."},
      {title:"She writes in another editor", body:"Priya drafts in <strong>Margin</strong>, a different editor. When she picks pro export, Margin asks Inkwell's server for the feature and gets a 402 that points to Inkwell's metadata, with monthly and annual Pro offers."},
      {title:"She signs in once", body:"Margin opens her browser to the License Server Inkwell uses. The consent screen names Margin, \"Inkwell Pro\", and a link to Inkwell's terms. She approves."},
      {title:"Margin gets a License Token", body:"Margin receives a License Token for pro export, <strong>bound to Margin's own key</strong> with DPoP. A copied token is useless anywhere else."},
      {title:"Inkwell's server decides", body:"When Priya exports, Margin calls Inkwell's export API with the token. Inkwell checks it and runs the export. A \"Pro\" badge in Margin proves nothing; the real check happens <strong>on Inkwell's side</strong>."},
      {title:"Cancel once, it ends everywhere", body:"If Priya cancels, the License Server revokes her access. Margin's token stops working when it expires, within the hour, along with any other editor she connected."}
    ], true) }}

    {{ storyDeck("bob", "Bob's story walkthrough", [
      {title:"Bob subscribes to a podcast feed", body:"Bob adds <strong>\"Sound and Signal\"</strong>, a music and culture podcast, to his player. Episode 12, <em>\"Why Vinyl Sounds Better (And Why It Doesn't)\"</em>, plays a 2-minute teaser. The full 57 minutes is for subscribers."},
      {title:"His player sees the offer", body:"The episode carries an <code>ope:offer</code>: <strong>\"Sound and Signal Plus, $3/month.\"</strong> The full episode sits in a Podcasting 2.0 <code>alternateEnclosure</code>. Players without OPE just play the teaser, as always."},
      {title:"Bob subscribes and signs in", body:"He subscribes through the show's checkout, then signs in from his player with the same OAuth flow every OPE app uses. The player needs no special deal with this show."},
      {title:"A token for every premium episode", body:"His <strong>License Token</strong> covers the whole premium catalog, not just Episode 12. The player stores it next to tokens from other shows."},
      {title:"The full episode downloads", body:"The player requests the full MP3 with the token. The server checks it and can hand back a <strong>signed URL that expires with the token</strong>, so links can't be passed around. Bob downloads it for his commute."},
      {title:"Switch players, keep the subscription", body:"Bob later tries another player. He signs in, it gets its own token, and every premium episode is there. <strong>No re-subscribing.</strong> His access follows him."}
    ], true) }}

    {{ storyDeck("school", "School course story walkthrough", [
      {title:"A school buys a course", body:"Maple Ridge School buys 200 seats in <strong>\"Woodworking 101\"</strong>, a course a creator sells on an online course platform. The school sends its class roster to the platform's License Server."},
      {title:"Students sign in with school accounts", body:"Jordan, a student, opens the course in whichever learning app they like and signs in with their school account. The License Server finds them on the roster."},
      {title:"Access comes from the school", body:"Jordan's <strong>License Token</strong> covers every lesson in the course and is marked as coming from the institution. Jordan never sees a price."},
      {title:"Short-lived by design", body:"School-issued tokens last <strong>an hour at most</strong> and refresh quietly. Every refresh checks that Jordan is still on the roster."},
      {title:"A student leaves", body:"Jordan transfers to another school, and Maple Ridge updates its roster. The License Server revokes Jordan's school access, and it ends <strong>within the hour</strong>. Nobody has to chase down which apps Jordan used."},
      {title:"Their own purchase still counts", body:"Had Jordan bought the course themselves, that purchase would take over and keep working. The school seat is a fallback, not a merge."}
    ], true) }}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Code Example -->
<section class="py-20 border-t border-zinc-900/5">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16 items-start">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 mb-4">Publish one document, use standard OAuth</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">A publisher adds one metadata document: for a whole subscription (every issue of a newsletter, say) or for a single gated item or API. It says who sells it, what's on offer, and which License Servers may issue access. Apps do the rest with ordinary OAuth.</p>
        <dl class="space-y-3">
          {% for item in [
            {k:"Discovery", v:"OAuth Protected Resource Metadata (RFC 9728) and Authorization Server Metadata (RFC 8414). No custom well-known URL."},
            {k:"Auth", v:"Authorization Code with PKCE, consent, and dynamic client registration"},
            {k:"Tokens", v:"One format: a signed JWT License Token, bound to the app's key with DPoP"},
            {k:"Offers", v:"Several per item (monthly, annual, student), in metadata and in feeds"},
            {k:"Web", v:"Sites unlock their own pages with HttpOnly cookies and 401/402 challenges"},
            {k:"Feeds", v:"ope:offer in RSS, Atom, and JSON Feed, for a whole feed or one item"}
          ] %}
          <div class="flex gap-3 text-sm">
            <dt class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 whitespace-nowrap">{{ item.k }}</dt>
            <dd class="text-zinc-600">{{ item.v }}</dd>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 lg:mt-0 bg-zinc-900 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-white/10"></span>
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-white/10"></span>
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-white/10"></span>
          <span class="ml-2 text-zinc-400 text-xs font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] truncate">/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/features/pro-export</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="p-5 overflow-x-auto m-0 text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed" tabindex="0" aria-label="Example resource metadata">{
  <span class="text-emerald-400">"resource"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"https://inkwell.example/features/pro-export"</span>,
  <span class="text-emerald-400">"authorization_servers"</span>: [<span class="text-amber-300">"https://license.lantern.example"</span>],
  <span class="text-emerald-400">"ope"</span>: {
    <span class="text-emerald-400">"version"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"0.2"</span>,
    <span class="text-emerald-400">"publisher"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"https://inkwell.example/"</span>,
    <span class="text-emerald-400">"offers"</span>: [
      {
        <span class="text-emerald-400">"id"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"pro-monthly"</span>,
        <span class="text-emerald-400">"name"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"Inkwell Pro"</span>,
        <span class="text-emerald-400">"payment"</span>: { <span class="text-emerald-400">"type"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"subscription"</span>, <span class="text-emerald-400">"amount"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"8.00"</span>,
                     <span class="text-emerald-400">"currency"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"USD"</span>, <span class="text-emerald-400">"period"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"P1M"</span> },
        <span class="text-emerald-400">"purchase_url"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"https://inkwell.example/pro"</span>,
        <span class="text-emerald-400">"terms"</span>: { <span class="text-emerald-400">"url"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"https://inkwell.example/terms/pro"</span> }
      }
    ]
  }
}</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Audience -->
<section class="py-20 border-t border-zinc-900/5" id="for-whom">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Who It's For</h2>
      <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Built for the entire ecosystem</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {% for card in [
        {t:"Publishers", d:"Keep full control of what you sell while making it work everywhere.", items:["Add ope:offer to the feeds you already publish","Gate articles, episodes, courses, features, or APIs","Publish resource metadata for each gated URL","Run a License Server, or use a platform's","Keep any payment processor and any login system","Migration paths for podcast hosts, newsletters, and course platforms"]},
        {t:"Apps & Browsers", d:"Feed readers, podcast players, editors, and browsers can unlock what people already hold, from any OPE publisher.", items:["Read ope:offer in RSS, Atom, and JSON Feed","Find metadata from a 401 or 402, or from a feed","Standard OAuth 2.0 with PKCE and DPoP","Reuse one token across a whole subscription","Show offers before anyone pays","A step-by-step Client algorithm in the spec"]},
        {t:"Platforms & License Servers", d:"Creator platforms, collectives, and institutions can issue access for many publishers at once.", items:["Issue for any publisher that lists you in its metadata","Host creators who don't have their own domain","Sell bundles across publishers, one token per publisher","Group and institutional access from a roster","Revoke by subscriber, app, or publisher","Keep a record of who held what, and when"]}
      ] %}
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-900/5 p-6">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">{{ card.t }}</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mb-4">{{ card.d }}</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 list-none p-0">
          {% for item in card.items %}
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-600 flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-700 mt-1.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">·</span> {{ item }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Entitlement Types -->
<section class="py-20 border-t border-zinc-900/5" id="entitlements">
  <span id="grants" aria-hidden="true"></span>{# keeps v0.1-era links to #grants working #}
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Flexible Access</h2>
      <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Three entitlement types, one token</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mt-3">OPE doesn't prescribe how access is earned; it standardizes how it's proven. Every Entitlement is one of three types with a few fields. Fourteen common patterns (subscription, gift, trial, and so on) are named aliases, but the protocol only validates three types.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-14">
      <div class="rounded-2xl p-6 bg-emerald-400/5 border border-emerald-400/20">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-500 w-2 h-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-emerald-700">access</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">The person may have this item, or everything in a collection. Covers subscriptions, single purchases, gifts, trials, rentals, bundles, and institutional seats: anything where the question is "can this person have this?"</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)]">coverage · duration · rental_expires_at · transferable · source</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl p-6 bg-amber-400/5 border border-amber-400/20">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="rounded-full bg-amber-500 w-2 h-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-amber-700">limit</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">The person may have items up to a quota that the publisher's server counts: metered paywalls, API allotments, a few free articles a month.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)]">coverage · kind · quota · period · remaining · source</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl p-6 bg-rose-400/5 border border-rose-400/20">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="rounded-full bg-rose-500 w-2 h-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-rose-700">status</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">The person has a standing that changes treatment: ad-free, patron, family-plan member, institutional affiliation. Status alone unlocks nothing; the publisher decides what it means.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)]">coverage · kind · source · group_id</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-10">
      <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Entitlement Builder</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600">Pick a preset to see how a named entitlement breaks down into a type and fields, or build your own and copy the JSON.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="entitlement-builder" aria-label="Entitlement builder widget" role="region"></div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{ '/js/entitlement-builder.js' | url }}"></script>

<!-- Compatibility -->
<section class="py-20 border-t border-zinc-900/5">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Compatibility</h2>
      <p class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Works with what you already use</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 mt-3">OPE is additive. Apps without OPE support see previews as usual.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {% for tag in ["RSS 2.0", "Atom", "JSON Feed", "Podcasting 2.0", "OAuth 2.0", "PKCE", "DPoP", "JWT", "RFC 9728", "RFC 8414", "RFC 7591", "RFC 7662", "HTTP 402", "RSL", "x402", "Stripe", "WordPress", "Ghost"] %}
      <span class="rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-zinc-600 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-900/10">{{ tag }}</span>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

